Let $k$ be a field and let $n > 2$ be an integer. Consider the polynomial ring $k[x_1,\dots,x_n]$ and the group $\mathrm{GA}_n(k)$ of polynomial automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}^n_k$, i.e., $k$-algebra automorphisms of $k[x_1,\dots,x_n]$. Inside $\mathrm{GA}_n(k)$, define:
\begin{itemize}
\item the affine subgroup $\mathrm{Aff}_n(k)$, consisting of automorphisms of the form $x_i \mapsto \sum_j a_{ij} x_j + b_i$ with $(a_{ij}) \in \mathrm{GL}_n(k)$ and $b_i \in k$;
\item the triangular (de Jonquières) subgroup $\mathrm{BA}_n(k)$, consisting of automorphisms of the form $x_i \mapsto c_i x_i + f_i(x_{i+1},\dots,x_n)$ with $c_i \in k^{\times}$ and $f_i \in k[x_{i+1},\dots,x_n]$;
\item the tame subgroup $\mathrm{TA}_n(k) := \langle \mathrm{Aff}_n(k), \mathrm{BA}_n(k)\rangle$.
\end{itemize}
Determine whether $\mathrm{Aff}_n(k)$ is a maximal subgroup of $\mathrm{TA}_n(k)$; that is, whether every subgroup $H$ with $\mathrm{Aff}_n(k) \subseteq H \subseteq \mathrm{TA}_n(k)$ satisfies $H = \mathrm{Aff}_n(k)$ or $H = \mathrm{TA}_n(k)$.

