Let $M$ be a smooth compact Riemannian manifold with boundary $\Sigma = \partial M$, and let $E, F \to M$ be Hermitian vector bundles over $M$. Let $A : C^\infty(M, E) \to C^\infty(M, F)$ be a general linear first-order elliptic differential operator. In a collar neighborhood $[0, \varepsilon) \times \Sigma$ of the boundary, write $A$ in the form
$$A = J(x)\bigl(\partial_x + B(x)\bigr) + \text{(lower-order terms)},$$
where $J(x)$ is a bundle isomorphism $E|_{\{x\}\times\Sigma} \to F|_{\{x\}\times\Sigma}$ and $B(x)$ is a first-order elliptic operator on $\Sigma$ (no assumption is made that $A$ is of Dirac type, nor that $J$ and $B$ are independent of $x$ or unitary/self-adjoint).

Determine to what extent the following structural results, classically established for Dirac-type operators with product structure near the boundary, persist for such general $A$:

(i) the existence of a canonical Calderón projection onto the Cauchy data space of $A$, given as a pseudodifferential projection with a transparent symbolic description;

(ii) the Lagrangian property of the Cauchy data space of $A$ with respect to a suitable symplectic structure on the boundary sections;

(iii) the existence of self-adjoint Fredholm extensions of $A$ realized by regular pseudodifferential boundary conditions;

(iv) a Cobordism Theorem expressing the vanishing of an index/signature invariant when $A$ extends across the boundary;

(v) continuous dependence of the Calderón projection, Cauchy data space, self-adjoint Fredholm extensions, and their spectral data under continuous variation of the operator $A$, the underlying domain $M$, and the boundary geometry.

Identify precisely which of (i)–(v) hold for arbitrary first-order elliptic $A$, which require additional hypotheses, and what minimal hypotheses on $A$ (weaker than Dirac-type with product structure) suffice.

