Let $(\widetilde{M}, J, g)$ be an almost Hermitian manifold of complex dimension $m$, with complex structure $J$ and Hermitian metric $g$. Recall that $\widetilde{M}$ is called a locally conformal Kähler manifold if there exists an open cover $\{U_\alpha\}$ of $\widetilde{M}$ and smooth functions $\sigma_\alpha : U_\alpha \to \mathbb{R}$ such that each local metric $e^{-2\sigma_\alpha} g|_{U_\alpha}$ is Kähler; equivalently, the fundamental 2-form $\Omega(X,Y)=g(X,JY)$ satisfies $d\Omega = \omega \wedge \Omega$ for a closed 1-form $\omega$ (the Lee form). A locally conformal Kähler space form $\widetilde{M}(c)$ is a locally conformal Kähler manifold of constant holomorphic sectional curvature $c$.

A submanifold $M$ of $\widetilde{M}$ is a CR-submanifold if there is a holomorphic distribution $\mathcal{D}$ (i.e. $J\mathcal{D}=\mathcal{D}$) and a totally real distribution $\mathcal{D}^\perp$ (i.e. $J\mathcal{D}^\perp \subset T^\perp M$) such that $TM = \mathcal{D} \oplus \mathcal{D}^\perp$. A CR-warped product submanifold is an isometric immersion of a warped product $M = M_T \times_f M_\perp$, where $M_T$ is a holomorphic submanifold (tangent space $\mathcal{D}$), $M_\perp$ is a totally real submanifold (tangent space $\mathcal{D}^\perp$), $f : M_T \to (0,\infty)$ is a smooth warping function, and the metric on $M$ is $g_{M_T} + f^2 g_{M_\perp}$.

For a unit tangent vector $X \in T_pM$, let $\mathrm{Ric}(X)$ denote the Ricci curvature of $M$ in direction $X$, and let $H$ denote the mean curvature vector of the immersion $M \hookrightarrow \widetilde{M}$.

Problem. Establish a sharp Chen–Ricci type inequality of the form
$$\mathrm{Ric}(X) \le \Phi\!\left(\|H\|^2,\, c,\, \dim M_T,\, \dim M_\perp,\, f,\, \nabla f\right)$$
for every unit tangent vector $X$ at every point of an arbitrary CR-warped product submanifold $M = M_T \times_f M_\perp$ isometrically immersed in:
(i) a locally conformal Kähler space form $\widetilde{M}(c)$;
(ii) the standard sphere $S^{2m}$ equipped with a suitable almost Hermitian (or other) structure of constant holomorphic sectional curvature;
(iii) more generally, any manifold endowed with a structure of constant holomorphic sectional curvature for which CR-warped products are defined.

In each case, explicitly determine the function $\Phi$ and characterize the equality case.

