A numerical semigroup is a subset S of the nonnegative integers that contains 0, is closed under addition, and has finite complement in the nonnegative integers. For a numerical semigroup S, define:

- the Frobenius number F(S) as the greatest integer not belonging to S;
- the genus g(S) as the cardinality of the set of nonnegative integers not in S;
- the embedding dimension e(S) as the cardinality of the minimal system of generators of S (equivalently, the cardinality of (S \ {0}) \ ((S \ {0}) + (S \ {0}))).

Determine whether every numerical semigroup S satisfies the inequality
    e(S) · g(S) ≤ (e(S) − 1) · (F(S) + 1).

