For a class X of groups, define the following class operators:
- H(X) = the class of all homomorphic images of groups in X;
- S(X) = the class of all groups isomorphic to a subgroup of some group in X;
- P(X) = the class of all groups isomorphic to an unrestricted direct product ∏_{i∈I} G_i of an arbitrary family (G_i)_{i∈I} of groups in X;
- P_f(X) = the class of all groups isomorphic to a direct product of a finite family of groups in X.

(By Birkhoff's HSP theorem, H(S(P(X))) is the variety of groups generated by X.)

Question: Is it true that for every class M consisting of metabelian groups (i.e., groups whose commutator subgroup is abelian), one has the inclusion
   H(S(P_f(M))) ⊆ S(H(P(S(M))))?

